# Canonical authorship for this repository.
#
# The work here is Ranvir Thind's. Agents — Claude Code, Cowork, Cursor, the
# drain bot — commit on his behalf, and have historically written themselves
# into the AUTHOR field. That field is what GitHub credits, what the
# contribution graph counts, and what `git blame` reports, so the owner was
# losing attribution on his own repository.
#
# The mapping is by EMAIL, not by name, deliberately: every agent so far has
# invented its own display name ("Claude", "Claude (Cowork)",
# "Claude (verify-and-build)", "loadoff-drain-bot") while sharing one address.
# Matching the address catches the next one too, without needing an edit.
#
# Read by `git log`, `git blame`, `git shortlog -sn`, and GitHub's contributor
# views. See AGENTS.md "Commit attribution" for the rule agents must follow at
# commit time — this file is the safety net, not the primary mechanism.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE: this file fixes DISPLAY in git tooling. GitHub's contribution
# graph does NOT read mailmap — it matches the raw commit author email to an
# account. So mailmap is the safety net for history already written; the real
# fix is committing with a GitHub-linked address in the first place, which is
# what scripts/git-identity.mjs sets.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> <commit@email>
# Normalises the display name on the owner's own hand-made commits, which
# carry the same address under the GitHub username rather than his full name.
